{% render 'bhd-page-header',
  family: 'Connect',
  parent: 'Partnerships',
  parent_url: '/pages/partnerships',
  eyebrow: 'Evidence Collaboration',
  title: 'Research Partnerships',
  intro: 'We are interested in research collaborations built around a useful question, appropriate methods and honest interpretation.',
  hero_image: 'https://images.pexels.com/photos/8533020/pexels-photo-8533020.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1800',
  hero_alt: 'Researchers in lab coats discussing findings in a modern laboratory'
%}

<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Research partnership standards">
  <div><strong>Question first</strong><span>Start with a defined problem or hypothesis, not a desired marketing conclusion.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Method matters</strong><span>Population, comparator, endpoints and analysis should match the question.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Status stays visible</strong><span>Planned, underway, completed and published work are different stages.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Why collaborate</p>
    <h2>Good research should still be useful when the result is inconvenient</h2>
    <p>The right collaborator helps define the question and the methods needed to answer it. We are more interested in durable evidence than a study designed to produce a favourable advertising sentence.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Research standard</span>
    <h3>Research is not pre-written marketing.</h3>
    <p>The protocol and interpretation should stand regardless of the direction of the result.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Ways to work together</p>
  <h2>From pilot questions to publishable studies</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
    <article><h3>Study design</h3><p>Question development, protocols, methods and appropriate endpoints.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Product evaluation</h3><p>Test formulations under defined conditions with suitable comparators.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Knowledge translation</h3><p>Interpret and communicate results after the work is complete.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Before data collection</p>
  <h2>Set the rules early</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Roles</h3><p>Define sponsor, investigator, analyst and operational responsibilities.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Ethics</h3><p>Follow applicable institutional and regulatory requirements.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Conflicts</h3><p>Disclose funding, product support and company involvement appropriately.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Publication</h3><p>Agree on how results, including unfavourable results, can be reported.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__brand-context">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Research inquiry</p>
    <h2>Bring a question, not just a collaboration label</h2>
    <p>Tell us the population, research question, proposed methods, institution or team, and what role you think Best Hydrate could play.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bhd-page__brand-actions">
    <a class="bhd-page__button" href="/pages/contact">Contact Us</a>
    <a class="bhd-page__button bhd-page__button--secondary" href="/pages/current-research">Current Research</a>
  </div>
</section>